---

HeaderFilterRegex: hipop/.*
WarningsAsErrors: '*'

Checks: # See https://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/list.html

  - cppcoreguidelines-*
  - modernize-*
  - performance-*

  # FIXME Significant legacy code refactoring would be necessary to address these warnings properly
  # (in particular, it would require to carefully review the integral types used to encode
  # the inputs and outputs of graph algorithm functions).
  - -cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions

  # FIXME Definitively worth enabling, but this would require to modify the graph data-structure
  # (to use smart pointers to manage Node/Link allocations - or even better to allocate them in-place
  # in the `mnodes`/`mlinks` maps), with impacts on the Python API. To be addressed in a dedicated change.
  - -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory

  # These checks require to use bounds-checked accessors on containers (e.g. `.at()` instead of `operator[]`).
  # Disabled because of the performance cost in hot loops, and because they raise false positives:
  # the index may be valid by the general logic of the algorithm, even if the checks can't deduce it.
  - -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access
  - -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index

  # Requiring all function definitions to follow the trailing-return-type syntax
  # conflicts with the habits of most C/C++ developers. Moreover, this brings nothing
  # in terms of performance, and the gain in terms of readability is questionable.
  # Reminder:
  # - classic syntax: `int function_name(...) { ... }`
  # - trailing-return-type syntax: `auto function_name(...) -> int { ... }`
  - -modernize-use-trailing-return-type
